================================================================================
Third-party data attribution
================================================================================

aml-filter screens names against the OFAC SDN (Specially Designated Nationals
and Blocked Persons) list.

    Specially Designated Nationals and Blocked Persons List (SDN List)
    Source:  U.S. Department of the Treasury,
             Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC)
             https://ofac.treasury.gov
             https://sanctionslist.ofac.treasury.gov
    Status:  Work of the U.S. Government, in the public domain
             (not subject to copyright in the United States).

aml-filter does NOT bundle or redistribute the SDN list. The list is not
included in this repository. The operator downloads it directly from the
official OFAC source at runtime and ingests it locally
(see docs/QUICKSTART.md). Always screen against the current official list —
the SDN list changes frequently, and a stale copy can miss or mis-match.

================================================================================
Ported third-party code
================================================================================

The @amlfilter/browser package's `./engine` tier
(frontend/packages/amlfilter-browser/src/engine) is a TypeScript port of
edge-proc's browser bundle-sync engine — the signed, content-addressed
sync state machine, OPFS store, fail-closed ed25519/sha256 crypto, and the
canonical manifest/wire format.

    edge-proc
    Source:  https://github.com/hseshadr/edge-proc
    License: MIT, Copyright (c) Harish Seshadri

